  "narrative": {
    "intro": "W W Grainger shows $295M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. W W Grainger has 146,995 awards this fiscal year to date and an average award size of $2K. W W Grainger's obligations fell 17.6% year over year. W W Grainger's FY26 obligations sit below the FY25 total of $358M and above the FY21 total of $198M, tracing a multi-year pattern that included FY22 at $210M, FY23 at $264M, and FY24 at $320M. The General Services Administration accounts for the vast majority of FY2026 to date obligations at $292M. The Home Centers NAICS market accounts for most FY2026 to date obligations at $293M. Other agencies and markets show materially smaller figures, such as the Department of Transportation at $909K and All Other Miscellaneous Electrical Equipment and Component Manufacturing at $396K. This mix shows concentration in routine supply and distribution channels via one primary agency and one primary NAICS market during the fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest federal buyers of W W Grainger?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration is the largest buyer at $292M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Transportation, Department of Justice, and Department of Health and Human Services follow with $909K, $427K, and $286K respectively. The Environmental Protection Agency is a smaller buyer at $20.2K in FY2026 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which markets account for W W Grainger federal sales?",
        "body": "Home Centers is the dominant NAICS market at $293M in FY2026 to date. All Other Miscellaneous Electrical Equipment and Component Manufacturing and Motor and Generator Manufacturing are next at $396K and $282K respectively. Other top NAICS markets include Industrial Supplies Merchant Wholesalers at $172K and Commercial and Service Industry Machinery Manufacturing at $106K."
      }
    ]
